I)</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Mann</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><article-title>Dignity and health: The UDHR's revolutionary first article</article-title><source>Health and Human Rights</source><year>1998</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>30</fpage><lpage>38</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/4065297</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Mann</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gostin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Gruskin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Brennan</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Lazzarini</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Fineberg</surname><given-names>HP</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Mann J, Gruskin S, Grodin MA, Annas GJ</person-group><article-title>Health and human rights</article-title><source>Health and Human Rights: A Reader</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>New York, Routledge</publisher-name><fpage>7</fpage><lpage>20</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Blumer</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><source>Symbolic Interactionism: Perspective and Method</source><year>1969</year><publisher-name>Berkeley, University of California Press</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Glaser</surname><given-names>BG</given-names></name><name><surname>Strauss</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><source>The Discovery of Grounded Theory: Strategies for Qualitative Research</source><year>1967</year><publisher-name>New York, Aldine Publishing</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Schatzman</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Maines DR</person-group><article-title>Dimensional analysis: notes on an alternative approach to the grounding of theory in qualitative research</article-title><source>Social organization and social process: Essays in honor of Anselm Strauss</source><year>1991</year><publisher-name>New York, Aldine De Gruyter</publisher-name><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>314</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Strauss</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><source>Qualitative Research for Social Scientists</source><year>1987</year><publisher-name>Cambridge, Cambridge University Press</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Charmaz</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Denzin NK, Lincoln YS</person-group><article-title>Grounded theory in the 21<sup>st </sup>century: applications for advancing social justice studies</article-title><source>The Sage Handbook of Qualitative Research</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Thousand Oaks, Sage Publications</publisher-name><fpage>507</fpage><lpage>535</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Jacobson</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><article-title>Dignity and health: a review</article-title><source>Social Science &#x00026; Medicine</source><year>2007</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>292</fpage><lpage>302</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.socscimed.2006.08.039</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B20"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Bayertz</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Bayertz K</person-group><article-title>Human dignity: philosophical origin and scientific erosion of an idea</article-title><source>Sanctity of Life and Human Dignity</source><year>1996</year><publisher-name>Dordrecht, Kluwer Academic Publishers</publisher-name><fpage>73</fpage><lpage>90</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B21"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Dales</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><article-title>A medieval view of human dignity</article-title><source>Journal of the History of Ideas</source><year>1977</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>557</fpage><lpage>572</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/2708687</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B22"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Kristeller</surname><given-names>PO</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Cassirer E, Kristkeller PO, Randall Jr, RH</person-group><article-title>Introduction</article-title><source>The Renaissance Philosophy of Man</source><year>1948</year><publisher-name>Chicago, University of Chicago Press</publisher-name><fpage>215</fpage><lpage>222</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B23"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Meyer</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><article-title>Kantian dignity and modern political thought</article-title><source>History of European Ideas</source><year>1987</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>319</fpage><lpage>332</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0191-6599(87)90005-2</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B24"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><article-title>Human dignity and the nature of society</article-title><source>The Philosophy Forum</source><year>1971</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>231</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B25"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Shell</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Kraynak RP, Tinder G</person-group><article-title>Kant on human dignity</article-title><source>Defense of Human Dignity: Essays for Our Times</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Notre Dame, University of Notre Dame Press</publisher-name><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>80</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B26"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Dillon</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Dillon RS</person-group><article-title>Introduction</article-title><source>Dignity, character, and self-respect</source><year>1995</year><publisher-name>New York, Routledge</publisher-name><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>49</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B27"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Gaylin</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><article-title>In defense of the dignity of being human</article-title><source>Hastings Center Report</source><year>1984</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6480335</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B28"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Sacks</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><source>The Dignity of Difference</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>London, Continuum</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B29"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Feldman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><article-title>Human dignity as a legal value &#x02013; Part I</article-title><source>Public Law</source><year>1999</year><volume>Winter</volume><fpage>682</fpage><lpage>702</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B30"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Feldman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><article-title>Human dignity as a legal value &#x02013; Part II</article-title><source>Public Law</source><year>2000</year><volume>Spring</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>76</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B31"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Seltser</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>D